# From the PACS to one MGZ per T1 series, in one play.
#
# Query a patient's MR studies, keep the series whose description says T1
# and not Gadavist, pull them into one new feed, and run the per-series
# pipeline on its root: pl-dymap makes one pl-freesurfer instance per series,
# each running mri_convert on the series' first DICOM file, so the four
# conversions run as four containers at once. The play ends when the feed
# has finished, or refuses after thirty minutes.
#
# Played from chell, logged in as a user who can reach the PACS:
#
#     play examples/t1_mgz.mise --param MRN=<mrn>
#
# PACS, LABEL and PIPELINE take the defaults below unless given with --param.
# PIPELINE is the pipeline's /bin name on BCH's CUBE; another CUBE names it
# differently. A pipeline run with no --previous runs at the feed node under
# the working directory, which is why the play does cd first.
@name         T1 series to MGZ, one per series
@description  Query a patient's MR series, keep the T1s, pull them into one new feed, and convert each to MGZ with FreeSurfer mri_convert in parallel.
@param        MRN
@param        PACS     = PACSDCM
@param        LABEL    = t1 cohort
@param        PIPELINE = FreeSurfer_8_2_0_mri_convert_per_series_DICOM_id291
@answers      FEED

T1=$(query PatientID:${MRN},Modality:MR --pacsserver ${PACS} | grep -i t1 | grep -vi gadavist)
FEED=$(pull ${T1} --new-feed "${LABEL}")
cd ${FEED.path}
${PIPELINE}
expect feed ${FEED.feedId} status eq finishedSuccessfully --within 30m
